{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788369517195,"sessionID":"ses_f9cdf1744ffeXefkzNuE7Vt14g","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9159f9e1d9d84d46","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view float-build-rust --repo kantord/toylang --comments"},"output":"invalid issue format: \"float-build-rust\"\n","metadata":{"output":"invalid issue format: \"float-build-rust\"\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view float-build-rust --repo kantord/toylang --comments","time":{"start":1788369517192,"end":1788369517194}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The issue is `float-build-rust`. The `gh issue view float-build-rust` failed with \"invalid issue format\". Let me try `gh issue view 149` since the JS float backend was issue-149. Actually, wait, the branch is `issue-float-build-rust`, and there's a commit \"Add Float for the JS backend (IEEE binary64, ADR 0007)\" and \"board: archive float-build (landed as 0c29911, issue-149 JS Float backend)\". \n\nLet me look at the issue list to find float-build-rust. But I was told `gh issue list` is denied. Hmm, but the brief says \"run `gh issue view float-build-rust` and read every comment before touching anything.\" It says KNOWN DENIALS include `gh issue list/search` but `gh issue view <N>` is allowed.\n\nThe issue `float-build-rust` doesn't work with gh issue view. Maybe I need `--repo kantord/toylang`. Let me try that.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063212d5e001410llmP72CNiOB","sessionID":"ses_f9cdf1744ffeXefkzNuE7Vt14g","messageID":"msg_063211ecd0015c67dMRLLRjfJC"}}
