{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788369550407,"sessionID":"ses_f9cdf1744ffeXefkzNuE7Vt14g","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b6e72a17527aa909","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git log --oneline -3 f22a806 && git merge-base --is-ancestor f22a806 HEAD && echo \"JS impl IS in HEAD\" || echo \"JS impl NOT in HEAD\""},"output":"f22a806 Add Float for the JS backend (IEEE binary64, ADR 0007)\n13d4098 Board: file gh:148, a parser bug found while researching the syntax-ergonomics round\nd00cb06 Cut the standing verbosity: policy once per session, boilerplate once per script\nJS impl IS in HEAD\n","metadata":{"output":"f22a806 Add Float for the JS backend (IEEE binary64, ADR 0007)\n13d4098 Board: file gh:148, a parser bug found while researching the syntax-ergonomics round\nd00cb06 Cut the standing verbosity: policy once per session, boilerplate once per script\nJS impl IS in HEAD\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git log --oneline -3 f22a806 && git merge-base --is-ancestor f22a806 HEAD && echo \"JS impl IS in HEAD\" || echo \"JS impl NOT in HEAD\"","time":{"start":1788369550404,"end":1788369550406}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The JS implementation is a comprehensive commit. Now, my task is to implement Float for the Rust backend only. The commit f22a806 already touched all files including emit_rs.rs (adding unreachable arms). So the shared infrastructure (ty, ast, parse, tir, check, float.rs) is already in place. My job is to make the Rust backend actually implement Float, i.e., update src/emit_rs.rs to emit Float code, and remove/adjust the unreachable arm.\n\nWait, but the commit f22a806 says \"The other six backends get unreachable arms for Float nodes and types\". So the shared parts (ty, ast, parse, tir, check, float.rs) are already done. The Rust backend emit_rs.rs has an unreachable arm. My task is to implement the actual Float emission in emit_rs.rs.\n\nBut the task says: \"Touch only what the Rust backend needs (ty, ast, parse, tir, check, emit_toylang, emit_rust, src/float.rs as needed)\". So it might be that the shared parts are already landed on main (in this worktree), and I just need to implement the Rust backend emit_rs.rs. But wait — the task says \"following float-build's JS implementation (already landed on main) as the reference for scope and shape.\"\n\nLet me check the current state of the worktree. Is f22a806 in the current HEAD? Let me check git log more carefully. The HEAD is 35f0748 \"board: archive float-build (landed as 0c29911, issue-149 JS Float backend)\". Hmm, f22a806 is \"Add Float for the JS backend\". Let me check if the current tree contains the JS implementation.\n\nLet me look at the current state of the files: src/emit_rs.rs, src/float.rs, src/tir.rs, src/ty.rs, src/parse.rs, src/ast.rs, src/check/mod.rs, tests/corpus/, tests/backend_rs.rs, tests/backend_js.rs.\n\nLet me first check whether the worktree is clean and whether the JS implementation is present.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06321bae9001xX0KVsJVmq2YQF","sessionID":"ses_f9cdf1744ffeXefkzNuE7Vt14g","messageID":"msg_06321905a001QaslV2BqDuj9AI"}}
